Changes made:

- **`extendedGcd` is now fully iterative** — replaced the recursive `extendedGcdHelper` with an inline loop tracking `(oldR, r)`, `(oldS, s)`, `(oldT, t)` pairs. Allocates exactly one `GcdResult` instead of O(log n).
- **Removed `extendedGcdHelper`** — the validate-once helper split was only needed because of recursion; with an iterative loop, `validate` runs once naturally at the top and the loop follows directly.

Changes from the last iteration:

```diff
diff --git a/euclidean_algorithms.java b/euclidean_algorithms.java
index 56ea4ad..ada4ce7 100644
--- a/euclidean_algorithms.java
+++ b/euclidean_algorithms.java
@@ -13,7 +13,16 @@ class EuclideanAlgorithms {
     // Finds gcd and Bézout coefficients: a*x + b*y = gcd
     static GcdResult extendedGcd(int a, int b) {
         validate(a, b);
-        return extendedGcdHelper(a, b);
+        int oldR = a, r = b;
+        int oldS = 1, s = 0;
+        int oldT = 0, t = 1;
+        while (r != 0) {
+            int q = oldR / r;
+            int tmp = r; r = oldR - q * r; oldR = tmp;
+            tmp = s; s = oldS - q * s; oldS = tmp;
+            tmp = t; t = oldT - q * t; oldT = tmp;
+        }
+        return new GcdResult(oldR, oldS, oldT);
     }

     static int gcd(int a, int b) {
@@ -27,12 +36,6 @@ class EuclideanAlgorithms {
         return (long) a / gcdHelper(a, b) * b;
     }

-    private static GcdResult extendedGcdHelper(int a, int b) {
-        if (a == 0) return new GcdResult(b, 0, 1);
-        GcdResult r = extendedGcdHelper(b % a, a);
-        return new GcdResult(r.gcd, r.y - (b / a) * r.x, r.x);
-    }
-
     private static int gcdHelper(int a, int b) {
         while (a != 0) { int t = a; a = b % a; b = t; }
         return b;
```

