Refactoring done. Changes made:

- **Renamed class** to `EuclideanAlgorithms` (plural, matching filename intent)
- **Added iterative GCD** (`gcdIterative`) alongside the existing recursive one — avoids stack overflow for large inputs
- **Added LCM** (`lcm`) which naturally follows from GCD; uses `long` return type to prevent overflow
- **Added input validation** — both GCD methods throw on negative inputs
- **Improved `main` output** — descriptive labels instead of printing a bare number

Changes from the last iteration:

```diff
diff --git a/euclidean_algorithms.java b/euclidean_algorithms.java
index a77756c..6b25f8d 100644
--- a/euclidean_algorithms.java
+++ b/euclidean_algorithms.java
@@ -1,13 +1,32 @@
-class EuclideanAlgorithm {
+class EuclideanAlgorithms {

-    static int findGCD(int a, int b) {
-        if (a == 0)
-            return b;
-        return findGCD(b % a, a);
+    static int gcdRecursive(int a, int b) {
+        if (a < 0 || b < 0)
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Inputs must be non-negative");
+        if (a == 0) return b;
+        return gcdRecursive(b % a, a);
     }
+
+    static int gcdIterative(int a, int b) {
+        if (a < 0 || b < 0)
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Inputs must be non-negative");
+        while (a != 0) {
+            int temp = a;
+            a = b % a;
+            b = temp;
+        }
+        return b;
+    }
+
+    static long lcm(int a, int b) {
+        if (a == 0 || b == 0) return 0;
+        return (long) a / gcdIterative(a, b) * b;
+    }
+
     public static void main(String[] args) {
         int a = 35, b = 15;
-        int g = findGCD(a, b);
-        System.out.println(g);
+        System.out.println("GCD(" + a + ", " + b + ") = " + gcdRecursive(a, b));
+        System.out.println("GCD(" + a + ", " + b + ") = " + gcdIterative(a, b) + " (iterative)");
+        System.out.println("LCM(" + a + ", " + b + ") = " + lcm(a, b));
     }
 }
```

